## §C0 -- state
HEAD `7d7e055`.  `src/devices/dev_lca.c` carries the `#518` fix UNCOMMITTED; the round is HELD on exactly
these three mutants.  Every table and instrument is committed under
`regress/artifacts/lcabadval/killtable_20260910/`.

## §C -- SETTLED PREMISES
S1. `fatal()` RETURNS; the process exit is a separate `exit(1)`.
S2. THE DEFECT `#518` fixed: `DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_ioc)` had six write arms of one shape -- store the value,
    then `fatal(); exit(1)` unless it equalled a tiny hard-coded set -- plus a `default:` arm that ended
    the process on any unlisted offset in either direction.  The manual (`_scratchpad/21066_66a_hrm.txt`,
    the Alpha 21066 HRM) makes several refused values LEGAL, and S6.4.14 REQUIRES the boot ROM to write
    zero to both window-base registers.
S3. THE FIX widened the six value guards to the manual's legal sets, made the default arm DECLINE with a
    latched announce (`lca_ioc_announce()`, eight `LCA_W_IOC_*` bits), and removed the exits.
S4. THE INSTRUMENT: `regress/lca_badval_probe.py`, 67 rows, 67/67 on the fix.  Frozen as
    `killtable_20260910/t4/lca_badval_probe.REPAIRED67.asrun.py`.
S5. THE FINAL TABLE, `killtable_20260910/t4/SCORES4.txt`, every log ending `LCABADVAL_DONE`:
        BASE                  67/67
        M43_mask1_widen       67/67   *** ESCAPES ***
        M44_mask1_field_idata 67/67   *** ESCAPES ***
        M45_base1_nosg        66/67   killed by `wbase1 sg`
        M46_conf_ann_wide     66/67   killed by `conf silent`
        M47_base1_widen       67/67   *** ESCAPES ***
        M48_wen_perreg        66/67   killed by `wen once`
        M49_def_narrow        66/67   killed by `def width`
    The three escapes ALSO escaped the 64-row table 3, where M45 escaped too and was then closed by a
    round-four row.
S6. MY READING, WHICH IS THE THING TO CHECK: all three escapes weaken the SECOND window's register pair --
    `W_MASK1` (M43, M44) and `W_BASE1` (M47) -- whose rows were added later and are thinner than the
    BASE0/MASK0 rows.  M43 widens the MASK1 value guard; M44 makes the MASK1 field come from `idata`
    rather than the fixed field; M47 widens the BASE1 value guard.  The mutator that built them is
    `killtable_20260910/t2/mutate518_t2.py`.

## THE QUESTIONS
1. **PREMISES AS QUESTIONS.**  Open `mutate518_t2.py` and the fix in `dev_lca.c`, and state what each of
   M43, M44 and M47 ACTUALLY edits, as an exact before/after.  Is S6's characterisation right?  In
