regress\artifacts\alphaswpctxreg\pass2_panel_20260908\ollama_kimi.txt:1:**VERDICT: No internal contradiction found — I re-derived all six witness cells from the probe's own program and the 2/4 → 4/4 table is arithmetically coherent. But the round is NOT complete: the floor's clause (d) rests partly on an unobserved initial-state premise (Q3), the `a0 land` row pins the implementation, not the architecture (Q2), and five factual claims embedded in the shipped fix comment are asserted, never exhibited — including another file-wide census claim, the same genre corrected last round.**
regress\artifacts\alphaswpctxreg\pass2_panel_20260908\ollama_kimi.txt:5:**Q1 — by-construction: acceptable, with one re-labeling.** (REASONED) The discrimination table is closed by arithmetic, not measurement, and that is fine: any product state reaches exactly one cell of `(v0, a0)`: correct `(C,N)` green; shipped `(S,C)` red twice; N-repair `(N,N)` red on `v0 ctx`; no-op `(S,N)` red on `v0 ctx`. The distinctness assert in-script makes "wrong repair accidentally hits C" impossible for any repair not returning old-ctx. The executed-path worry (did call 2 even run?) is already extinguished pre-fix by `a0 land = C`, which requires call 2's handler to have fired. **Caveat:** clause (b) — the measured shipped-defect run — and clause (d) cover *different points* in repair space; (d) should stop borrowing (b)'s "measured" weight. A built `v0=N` mutant would add one thing only: cross-validation that the PREFIX/POSTFIX labels weren't swapped. That is calibration, not floor logic. Not owed.
regress\artifacts\alphaswpctxreg\pass2_panel_20260908\ollama_glm.txt:1:**VERDICT: The fix is sound on the packet's own showing, and Q1's clause (d) is discharged by inspection, not by argument — no built mutant is owed. But the shipped comment engraves four premises the packet never exhibits (one of them carries the "correct AND sufficient" claim), the probe leaves the entire load-new-context/invalidate tail of `swpctx` unwitnessed, and the `a0 land` row scores as required a behavior the comment itself says is not owed.**
regress\artifacts\alphaswpctxreg\pass2_panel_20260908\ollama_glm.txt:19:**(d) by construction is acceptable here, and I'd push back on calling it an argument.** READ: the row is a constant equality, `v0_final` against `"0x%x" % CTX_C`; the three oracle constants are pairwise distinct and the probe *asserts* their distinctness; both sides use the same formatter, so no hex-width accident; and every other row is value-blind with all parse failures failing RED (`printed` returns `"absent"`, which fails every comparison). The only route to GREEN is the parsed value equaling C exactly. Of the three oracle cells, S is measured (2/4 pre-fix — the handler-never-writes-v0 world) and C is measured (4/4); the N cell needs nothing but `N ≠ C`. A built `v0 = a0` mutant would add only "the probe runs on a v0-writing build," and runnability is already evidenced twice. **A mutant is owed when the row's predicate could be satisfied by a wrong repair ("v0 changed"); this row's predicate cannot be.** The round owes one sentence recording that discharge, so pass 3 doesn't re-litigate. Caveat on scope: this discharges wrong-repair vacuity for the *return-value* contract only — see Q2.
