regress\artifacts\lcashiftub\pass2_c7d7414\codex.txt:1126:GXEMUL-SEC/regress\pass2_ledger.tsv:43:a636a33	2026-08-21	panel_20260821_185116	8 fired: 7of7 scriptable answered + opus5 measuring seat; fable5 DELIBERATELY NOT FIRED (owner directive), not a seat failure	7of7	SHIP-WITH-CHANGES, applied before this receipt was filed. 8 seats fired, 7of7 scriptable answered (codex 16.5KB, agy 11.2KB, kimi 44.8KB, grok 8.3KB, glm 7.3KB, deepseek 2.9KB, minimax 7.5KB) plus the opus5 measuring seat; fable5 DELIBERATELY NOT FIRED per the owner's standing deprioritisation, recorded as a deliberate omission and never as agreement. Verdicts split 3 SOUND / 3 DEFECT-IN-DETECTOR / 1 format-miss. *** THE PANEL CAUGHT THE ROUND REPEATING ITS OWN MISTAKE AT TWO SITES IT HAD JUST FIXED AT A THIRD. ***  The round's own mutation run measured R2 vacuous -- it carried the ACCEPTED resource select, so after a `return`->`break` fall-through the RS arm was happy and exactly one diagnostic printed either way. R2 and R3 were rebuilt with an illegal RS. R1 WAS NOT, and the comment left on the TS arm CLAIMED IT WAS COVERED: 'a break here falls through to the RS switch, which for most values complains too' -- true of most values, and R1 was using the one that does not. A WRONG RECORD, in the same file, in the same session. THE KEEPER: FIXING TWO OF THREE SIBLINGS AND WRITING A COMMENT ASSERTING THE THIRD WAS COVERED IS HOW A WRONG RECORD SHIPS. *** THE RS VARIANT IS THE SERIOUS ONE BECAUSE IT PUTS exit(1) BACK. ***  With `return` at the RS default the function leaves before `if (cause_interrupt)`. Replace it with `break` and that site becomes reachable from ALL SIXTEEN resource-select encodings instead of the one X1 pins -- host death this diff removed, restored by one keyword. No reject row could see it, because every one had IE clear. MEASURED after the seat said plainly 'not recompiled here': TS `break` 16/16 SURVIVED, RS `break` 16/16 SURVIVED, and its third remark -- `fatal`->`debug` as 'one identifier and also 16/16' -- measured true as well, invisible to every row because they all single-step, where debug() prints exactly like fatal(). CLOSED IN-ROUND RATHER THAN FILED, on the vacuity floor: the RS variant re-exposes exit(1) on a guest-reachable path, so the detector fails the 'verbatim reinstatement at every fixed site' clause for that site in its `break` form. That is not coverage debt. Three rows answer it -- R1 re-valued, R7 added (an illegal RS WITH IE SET: alive when the arm returns, dead the moment it falls through), and F1 added (free-running, where debug() goes silent and fatal() does not). ELEVEN MUTANTS, NO SURVIVORS, re-measured: TS/DM/SM/RS return->break -> R1/R2/R3/R7; fatal->debug -> F1; TS/SM/RS exit(1) restored -> R1/R3/R4 R5 R7 L2 F1; DM and TS mask growth -> R4 R5 A1 L2 and A4 L1; latch whole-register/no-encoding/no-channel -> L1/L2/L3; IE site repaired -> X1. Clean tree 18/18. FIVE ROWS WERE MEASURED VACUOUS ACROSS THE ROUND AND REBUILT, each with confident reasoning beside it: R2 (accepted RS), L1 (second store a BIT-SUBSET of the first, so a whole-register latch computed fresh==0 and stayed silent), R5 (byte-identical to R4), R6 (proves channel 3 REACHES the guard, not that the latch DISTINGUISHES channels -- L3 added for that), and R1. SCOPE HELD AT FOUR SITES BY PANEL RULING: two pass-1 seats independently put :486 (CHCR_IE) in its own round, because it is an unimplemented FEATURE rather than an unimplemented ENCODING and needs an interrupt-delivery oracle. PINNED by row X1, which requires that site to still be fatal -- so the gate reddens the day it is repaired and names the row. A scope decision no row asserts is indistinguishable from an oversight. A PASS-1 QUESTION REFUTED ITSELF AND FOUND A SEPARATE DEFECT: asked whether a copy loop runs before the RS switch, the answer is that THERE IS NO COPY LOOP -- sh4_dmac_transfer() writes nothing to guest state on any path, and the one arm that returns normally is `(void)sar; (void)dar;` under the comment 'No transfer is done here!'. That made the fix trivially safe and surfaced sh4dmanop: a guest polling for DMA completion already waits forever, before and after. Gates: gate_sh_rounding PASS (56 checks, was 54), run singly.
regress\artifacts\lcashiftub\pass2_c7d7414\codex.txt:1127:GXEMUL-SEC/regress\pass2_ledger.tsv:51:3ff2138	2026-08-22	panel_20260822_155826	9 fired, 9 answered: 7of7 scriptable + opus5 + fable5	9of9	SHIP-WITH-DETECTOR-GROWN, applied before this receipt. 9 seats fired, 9 answered: 7of7 scriptable (codex 25.7KB, agy 9.0KB, grok 6.6KB, kimi 74.2KB, glm 4.4KB, deepseek 2.8KB, minimax 6.2KB) plus opus5 (measuring) and fable5 (records). Verdicts 3 SHIP / 4 DEFECT-IN-DIFF among the scriptable seats, DEFECT from both agent seats -- and EVERY dissent was correct. *** THE ASK-AGAIN PRODUCED FOUR ESCAPES FROM ONE ASK, its best yield on record, and the fourth was a SHIPPED WRONG RECORD with witnessed corruption behind it. *** QACR (opus5, measured): gate_sh_rounding.sh called `sq at0 qacr` 'the regression guard: the QACR composition must be exactly as before'. MEASURED FALSE -- the composition can be DELETED OUTRIGHT and that row stays green. Two structural reasons: NO row had ever written QACR0/QACR1 and dev_sh4.c seeds them nowhere, so the term was identically ZERO in every row; and every operand had bit 5 SET so sq_nr was 1 in all ten rows and QACR0 was never consulted, ever. The escape is WITNESSED guest-visible corruption -- with AT=0 the destination area comes entirely from QACR. #454 made the edit MORE likely by adding three comments saying QACR 'takes no part'. Three rows added; 34/34 fixed, 31/34 composition-deleted, 31/34 qacr0/qacr1-swapped. Fixed in-round as L4 because the wrong record was live in the SHIPPED tree. SQMD (codex): flags = (mmucr & SQMD) ? FLAG_WRITEFLAG : 0 passed all 31 because every row left SQMD clear. `sq pr00 rdok` now sets it -- privileged, so SQMD cannot bar it. MEASURED 31/31 fixed, 30/31 mutant. SEED COLLISION (fable5): change the evt rows' no-exception seed from 0x999 to 0x040 and `sq miss evt` can no longer tell a raised code from a surviving seed, silently reopening the FLAG_NOEXCEPTIONS payload-at-physical-zero escape. Fixed by an ASSERTION rather than a convention -- every EXPEVT code is a multiple of 0x20 so the seed must not be; an enumerated list would go stale on the first added row. Controlled both ways. PROT_LD (deepseek, and kimi named the same class at pass 1): corrupting EXPEVT_TLB_PROT_LD is invisible because every SH TLB row runs privileged and PR=00 permits a privileged read. FILED as shprotld, not fixed: it mutates the general TLB table rather than this call site, the detector is already above the vacuity floor, and the user-mode row that closes it carries a measured trap. FOUR CITATION DEFECTS IN THE ROUND'S OWN DIFF, all found by fable5 and all verified by opening the target: two unfilled #NNN; cpu_sh.c:690 which is :688; both manual ranges overshooting by one line; and memory_sh.c:348-351, WHICH THIS DIFF ITSELF FALSIFIED by inserting 26 lines above it -- exactly the class the round was correcting. AND ONE OVERCLAIM DISPROVED BY THE ROUND'S OWN DETECTOR (codex): the memory_sh.c comment said an SQ page now raises 'no MMU fault of any kind', while `sq miss evt` observes a read-type TLB miss at 0x040 on the fixed build. Only the WRITE-side pair disappears. Corrected, and the correction says so. SIBLING SWEEP: seven in-repo locations asserted the old reading, not the three the design named -- fable5 found four more (cpu_sh_instr.c:3738, CHANGELOG:3806-3825 and :13639-42, OUTSTANDING_BUGS:418-429 and :437-439) plus a stale .pyc and three build-tree copies. All discharged; the two CHANGELOG blocks annotated in place rather than rewritten, and deliberately NOT overcorrected -- that retrospective's address-composition, exception-XOR-store and [25:6] conclusions were later CONFIRMED by the real manual and stand. Gates: gate_sh_rounding PASS (70 checks, was 62 at round start) run singly; detector 34/34; build rc=0 zero warnings; all five trees cmp-identical to GXEMUL-SEC.
regress\artifacts\lcashiftub\pass2_c7d7414\codex.txt:1128:GXEMUL-SEC/regress\pass2_ledger.tsv:55:7e5c0f6	2026-08-23	panel_20260823_030159	9 fired, 9 answered; no seat down	9of9	SHIP-WITH-CHANGES, applied before this receipt. 9 fired, 9 answered -- NO SEAT DOWN. codex returned 25,756 bytes, squarely inside its own quota-wall size range, and was cleared by CONTENT not size (zero quota keywords). grok and glm gave no formatted VERDICT line: FORMAT misses, recorded as such, never as agreement. *** THE PASS CHANGED THE ROUND SUBSTANTIALLY AND THE STRONGEST FINDING WAS A SELF-CONTRADICTION IN THE DIFF. *** grok: the function's OWN header table still declared `Reserved` in ipra[3:0], iprb[7:4] and iprc[7:4] -- the exact three cells the new code maps, twenty lines below -- so a reader trusting it puts SCIF back on INTPRI08. Also: `of all the Table 19.6 sources only SCIF is drivable at all` is FALSE, TMU asserts at dev_sh4.c:585 from a host timer, and THE PROBE'S OWN HEADER carried the accurate synchronous-vs-host-timer wording the whole time. Also: int_to_assert/int_level were exposed with a justification NO ROW HONOURS -- removed, seconded independently by minimax. *** FABLE5 (liveness token returned) CAUGHT FOUR CITATION ERRORS IN THIS ROUND'S OWN CORRECTIONS, and #457 had shipped four of its own: :40142->:40144; the source-row range :40083 EXCLUDED the H-UDI row at :40081 that it was citing; :40247->:40248; and dev_sh4.c:2379-2381->:2386-2388, WHICH THIS ROUND SHIFTED ITSELF by inserting a comment above the line minutes after citing it correctly. Root cause found and carried: `sed -n 'A,Bp'` prints lines WITHOUT numbers so the number is counted by hand -- use grep -n or awk NR. *** OPUS5 FOUND THE ONE ESCAPE THAT WAS NOT COVERAGE DEBT, BY COMPILING IT. *** m_sciftxonly narrows the IPRC SCIF loop to TXI alone, one identifier, and MEASURED 14/14. Unlike every other escape it reaches a LIVE line: SCIF RXI 0x720 is asserted by dev_sh4.c:250-256 on RIE && DR, connected :1912 -- CONSOLE INPUT on landisk. Measured iprio_720 = 0x1f/delivered on the fix vs 0x10/refused on the mutant, so the mutant silently deletes console input with the gate green. Fixed in-round as a MEASURED FALSE PASS on live functionality; four rows now pin the loop's whole membership. opus5 also independently rebuilt m_iprdread and reproduced 13/14 red-on-`iprd hold`, discharging vacuity-floor (b) from a second hand; found m_irqramp passes the TWELVE-row detector and is killed only by the IPRD pair; and supplied the SH7750 fixed-levels footnote at :39956-39959, a STRONGER IPRD arm than the round or any other seat had. ONE REFUTED: deepseek required, as its ship condition, `SH4_INTEVT_SCIF_TEI` -- a constant that DOES NOT EXIST. sh4_exception.h:104-107 defines four SCIF vectors ending in TXI, so the loop already covers all four and the edit would not compile; it had transplanted SCI's vector set onto SCIF. Right about everything else. THE ASK-AGAIN (one, capped) returned grok's m_iprdread: the round's CENTRAL DECISION -- declining IPRD -- was defended only by a comment. `iprd hold` + `iprd ctl` now pin it, MEASURED 13/14. Everything found past the cap was FILED, not fixed: eight escape shapes as sh4iprunpinned, plus sh4standinglower, sh4pcic15, sh4irlm. THE DETECTOR GREW TWICE INSIDE ONE PASS 2 (12->14->18), each growth forced by a mutant the previous size could not see -- queued to the flagship regress seat as a RULE QUESTION: is that the stopping rule working or #392 with better paperwork? KILL TABLE, each red on exactly the row built for it: m_iprconly 10/12 (iprb wdt, ipra rtc), m_nortc 11/12 (ipra rtc), m_norescan 11/12 (raise), m_iprdread 13/14 (iprd hold), m_sciftxonly 15/18 (scif eri/rxi/bri, with scif txi correctly GREEN). ONE SELF-INFLICTED GATE FAILURE, caught by the gate: a backslash-continuation written through a nested heredoc put the literal characters 
regress\artifacts\lcashiftub\pass2_c7d7414\codex.txt:1129:GXEMUL-SEC/regress\pass2_ledger.tsv:62:ba30e64	2026-08-23	panel_20260823_140419 panel_20260823_213058	#461 both default: arms of the GD-ROM device ended the host process	9of9	SHIP-WITH-CHANGES, every change applied before this receipt. THREE PANELS on one round -- pass 1 (design), pass 2 (diff), pass 3 (final state) -- plus two flagship reviews. All nine seats answered at least one; NO SEAT DOWN at pass 3, and grok was recorded as MID-ANSWER rather than as a failure, which is a distinction this project has mis-made before. *** THE ROUND WAS HELD UNCOMMITTED BY OWNER DECISION ACROSS TWO FABLE USAGE-LIMIT FAILURES, AND THE HOLD PAID FOR ITSELF FOUR TIMES. *** codex returned DO NOT SHIP on pass 2 for a write alias THE FIX WOULD HAVE CREATED: the DMA tail stores through truncating division, so a declined byte write at +0x05 landed in dma_reg[1], the DMA destination, with the same alias reaching length (+0x09) and count (+0x0d). `case 0x18` reads count and enable to arm, then destination and length -- so a guest could arm and AIM a transfer entirely through declined offsets, bypassing every check the implemented cases perform. Pre-fix each of those exited. The round's own comment claimed the opposite. Closed by returning before BOTH tails on any unaligned access, whose soundness is an INJECTIVITY PROOF -- on multiples of 4 the map off -> off/4 is injective, so an aligned offset reaching the arm cannot share an index with any implemented case, because if it did it would BE that case -- and a seat re-derived that proof independently before it was believed. opus5 then built FOUR mutants that scored a full 27/27 against the detector: `& 3` -> `& 1` (a 16-bit store at +0x06 is 2-byte aligned, architecturally legal, and re-opens the alias); the guard restricted to MEM_WRITE (the read half the comment claimed and no row pinned); and each arm keyed into the OTHER window's latch array, one of which additionally writes past the shorter row onto dma_reg[0] -- invisible to ASan, being member-to-member inside one malloc. *** `dma alias`, THE ROW WRITTEN TO PIN THAT VERY REPAIR, WAS STRUCTURALLY BLIND TO THE FIRST *** because it uses an ODD address that both guard forms drop: a row written from the fix's intent tests the intent, not the boundary. That measurement is what the owner adopted as vacuity-floor clause (d) NULL-REPAIR RED. fable5 found the round's UNDISCHARGED L3 OBLIGATION, which no other seat named across two full panels: `accept8` exists for the control window because three narrowing mutants scored full marks, and the DMA window got the same fatal->survive fix with NO accept row -- delete `case 0x18:` and the DMA trigger dies silently forever, where before this round that deletion was a loud exit on first touch. It also found SEVEN wrong records, every one confirmed by grep or by reading before being acted on; the sharpest was a gate comment boasting its numbers were 'MEASURED at the final row count, not carried over' which was ITSELF carried over and false three ways -- the third generation of the frozen-number defect, inside the sentence memorialising the first two. PASS 3 WAS OWED AND NEARLY MISSED: pass 2 reviewed a 27-ROW detector, and the diff had since gained five rows, the GDROM_UNIMPL_FIRST macro, the injectivity proof, a diagnostic correction and the unaligned guard. Reviewed whole for the first time it produced three real findings: glm found the macro's true constraint (`sizeof(arr) * 8` is element-type-AGNOSTIC so it computes a correct BIT COUNT for any array, while gdrom_unimpl_first indexes `bits[k >> 5]` through a uint32_t* -- a uint8_t[] gives the right count and the wrong indexing, the worst combination because the obvious sanity check passes; codex flagged the same brittleness independently); glm and minimax both asked that the CONTROL window's structural safety be written down; and codex asked for an explicit write-direction guard around the DMA arming, which was CHECKED IN TWO MINUTES rather than judged and found already satisfied 140 lines above (`idata` is declared = 0 and assigned only under `if (writeflag == MEM_WRITE)`), so no code change -- but the probe comment now names the real property, because a guard 140 lines from what it protects is correct and hard to see. glm's request for a `& 3` guard on the control arm was DECLINED WITH A REASON: that arm has no store tail, so the guard would be DEAD CODE, and this round already rejected one dead bounds check for exactly that. deepseek was the only seat asked for a new 32/32 mutant that said plainly it could not find one AND enumerated what it had eliminated -- an honest empty result with its search space named, from a packet-fed seat. kimi named four measurements rather than asserting a verdict it had not earned; M4 was checked immediately and confirmed (:749 and :889 are character-identical index expressions, so `return 1` -> `break` has no silent read-path variant). MEASURED: 9/32 pre-fix and 32/32 post-fix, BOTH at 32 rows (pre461f.out) -- the heading had said 8/32 'both MEASURED' seventeen minutes BEFORE that run started, and the carried 8 was wrong as well as unmeasured, which is why the carrier now requires a score claim to name its log. Every row added because a mutant escaped is discharged by a measured kill: m_deldma18 31/32 (dma accept), m_wrcross 31/32 (both windows), m_delalign 29/32 (three rows; clause (d)'s own shape), m_dmarevert 22/31 (floor clause (b) at BOTH fixed sites). Gate 10 PASS at 190 checks run alone, 179 before. Four trees cmp-identical; build rc=0, zero warnings. The 32/32 re-verification after the final comment-only edits held under SEVEN concurrent emulators, which makes it a stronger result than a quiet-machine run.
regress\artifacts\lcashiftub\pass2_c7d7414\codex.txt:1130:GXEMUL-SEC/regress\pass2_ledger.tsv:64:96196f3	2026-08-23	panel_20260823_213058	#461 aftermath: goto-fail shape, two measured-false claims, five escapes	9of9	COMMENT- AND RECORDS-ONLY on src/, and its content IS a measuring seat's pass-2 output on ba30e64, so no new panel is owed and none was fired -- the disposition already on record for 2965aa1, e4390ea and 029a137, written down rather than taken silently. The seat that produced it did 18 builds and 20 probe runs against source byte-identical to ba30e64. *** IT FOUND FIVE 32/32 ESCAPES, AND THE HEADLINE ONE GOES AROUND #461'S STRUCTURAL DEFENCE RATHER THAN THROUGH IT. *** E1 transposes the word- and bit-index expressions in gdrom_unimpl_first; MEASURED TWICE with a standalone probe, four DECLINED 32-bit READS in the CONTROL window write 1 into dma_reg[1], [2], [3] and [5] -- exactly case 0x18's arming condition, reached from the wrong window entirely. bits is a uint32_t[2]; bits[k & 31] runs to index 31 and dma_reg[0] sits six words past it; ASan is blind, member-to-member inside one malloc. THE BOUNDS GUARD STILL PASSES because k is still off/4 < nkeys -- the round's defence protects the BOUND, E1 lives in the INDEX, and no row was on the index. The seat was honest about its own finding's limit: each HALF of the transposition dies alone, because the rows measure key DISTINCTNESS and a transposition preserves that exactly. FILED as gdromkeyindex, not fixed -- the stopping rule reserves in-round fixes for a measured false pass or a wrong record, and #461's detector is above the vacuity floor on all four clauses, so this is coverage debt (the #447 disposition, reached by the seat itself). Six closing rows are written and validated at 38/38. *** AND IT FOUND A GOTO-FAIL SHAPE I HAD INTRODUCED ONE COMMIT EARLIER, as a courtesy note on in-flight work rather than as a finding. *** 029a137 put a 39-line comment BETWEEN `if (writeflag == MEM_WRITE)` and its unbraced statement. Behaviourally harmless -- a comment is not a statement -- but anyone adding a line after it would believe they were inside the `if`, and it reads as though the `if` has no body. No gate catches that shape. TWO CLAIMS OF MINE MEASURED FALSE, both by building rather than reading: the uint8_t[] caution said the wrong-indexing mistake is silent 'because the obvious sanity check passes' -- both uint8_t[] and uint64_t[] are HARD BUILD ERRORS at both call sites (GCC 15.2.1; -Wincompatible-pointer-types has been an error by default since GCC 14), so it is a portability caution and not a silent-corruption hazard; and the header's 'the extent and the guard are the same identifier' was true when written and FALSE at HEAD, with its own correction 150 lines below and nothing pointing at it. AND ONE THAT WOULD HAVE COST A ROUND: OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md still read '### gdromdefault -- open' after ba30e64 shipped it and a7b103d was titled 'close gdromdefault'. The carrier's first-stop procedure reads that file as the live queue. A sweep then found SIX MORE stale headings; section W now checks that direction, negative-controlled both ways.
regress\artifacts\lcashiftub\pass2_c7d7414\codex.txt:1131:GXEMUL-SEC/regress\pass2_ledger.tsv:107:3403c01	2026-08-27	panel_20260827_154xxx+opus5/fable5 Agent seats	#482 wdc: the abort row could not say which state gated the abort	9of9	9 of 9; kimi CLI 403-walled, COVERED by kimi-k3:cloud. RATIFIED by both flagship seats, which then built the SAME escape independently: `if (write_in_progress || atapi_cmd_in_progress)` -- 'precisely the repair a maintainer writes after reading the four rows', defeating all four because each arms one of those flags. The killing state (ring non-empty, both flags clear) is GUEST-REACHABLE: the #464 tenant test gates only the one-shot diagnostic while wdc_addtoinbuf() sits outside it. *** A ROW SET CAN BE INDIVIDUALLY CORRECT AND COLLECTIVELY MISLEADING -- each of the four is right; together they teach the wrong property, and nothing in the vacuity floor catches that. *** Also: the composite-row weakness was measured twice against my own reasoning (a row arming MORE state is WEAKER against guard over-restriction, since more state satisfies more guards); L4 on the witness kind (`harness:`, not 'reproduction' -- named by both seats); L1 in row_srst_aborts_pkt_only, which armed a field it never asserted, flagged by my own sibling audit and dismissed as a false positive. The generator was destroyed mid-round by a seat writing the same filename in the shared scratchpad; reconstructed, marked as such, and verified to reproduce the table.
regress\artifacts\lcashiftub\pass2_c7d7414\codex.txt:1132:GXEMUL-SEC/regress\pass2_ledger.tsv:114:fb0cc78	2026-08-29	panel_20260829_072258 + panel_20260829_133206 + opus5/fable5 Agent seats	#490 GD-ROM handle_command: two guest-reachable host kills, plus a wsl-dollar hook	9of9	TWO nine-seat panels on this diff, both recorded with their dirs cited. *** FULL ON THE PRODUCT EDIT, PARTIAL ON ONE AXIS, AND THE AXIS IS NAMED RATHER THAN GLOSSED. *** At panel time `regress/gdrom_decline_probe.py` was UNTRACKED, so it was absent from `git diff` and the numstat -- the codex seat said so in its own words: 'this is a working-tree review, not yet a SHA-keyed receipt.' The seats read the file; git could not. It is tracked as of this SHA. Recorded per 84765ec's precedent, which refused the same stretch. PASS 2 (panel_20260829_072258): all nine answered. SUPPLEMENTARY (panel_20260829_133206): all nine, opus5 landing last and *** FINDING THREE MEASURED ESCAPES IN THE COMPILE-TIME ASSERT *** that the shipped `+` form closes -- eight states x both operator forms, on the real file, md5s per source state. The mechanism is the vacuity floor's ANCHOR RULE one level down, inside a constant expression: an OR test 'proves coverage relative to a count derived from the possibly aliased last enum value; it does not independently count masks', so an enum-side alias drags NBITS down and the equality RE-BALANCES. A sum cannot absorb a duplicate. The `+` form had already landed from fable5's multi-bit finding and is STRICTLY BETTER than the seat's own `SUM == OR` proposal, which would have lost both completeness cases; the seat recorded its superseded proposal rather than dropping it. TWO L4s CORRECTED, and the second is the lesson: the comment claimed 'MEASURED IN FIVE STATES, controls preserved at assert_controls_20260829/' while that script tests `|` and the file ships `+` -- the cited controls backed a declaration the file no longer contained. I fixed that and did NOT grep for siblings, so the SAME wrong record survived in CHANGELOG.md and had to be found again by a backward-search hunt. That is mechanical rule 2 broken by the round that cites it. `stale how` DISCHARGED by two routes answering different questions: my rotted-packet mutant moved FOUR rows (60/60 -> 56/60), proving the row is FAILABLE against the wanted-equals-failure objection; the seat's main.c mutant moved ONE (60/60 -> 59/60), proving SOLE CARRIAGE. The seat's is the discharge; mine is not, and the round says so. E2/E3 filed as gdromlatchcross WITH their measured rows already built (base 22/22, each mutant 21/22, orthogonal), so the follow-up arrives as an implementation rather than a hunt -- plus a rename warning: the seat's own candidate name is exactly 14 chars = the gate column width, the padded-column trap, which it caught because its own summary table printed blank while the FAIL list did not.
