 errdiv0, errpriv, errunimpl, ovfc, indclr, umisalign, udiv0, unimpl, uovf, bounds(?), div0, usertb, resid50, resid127, usfu1, sfu1h, vbrtb, m88kexcsfu1 (a control?), dslot?... The exact 41 aren't fully inlined, but enough.\n\nNow, candidate clean-sweep mutants. Let me think about what the composite now covers and what the disclosed gaps are (the docstring's \"Does NOT catch\" and \"still disclosed\" lists):\n\nStill disclosed: {class} x {delay_slot} beyond DIV0 (m88kdslotshadow); M_DELAYALWAYS; vectors 0..3's switch-1 and tail arms (m88kexchwtraps); DMT contents; SSBR; fcr2/4/5; first-exception SFU1 (m88kexcsfu1; SFU1_IMPRECISE 115 likewise); exact INFO; `implemented = is_trap` at BOUNDS/ERROR (equivalent today, m88ktbnd); the {MODE} x {SFRZ} x {class} triple for MISALIGNED/OVERFLOW/DIV0 (clause e); an exemption of a single residual vector other than 11/50/127 from the fallback (a value the body never tests as a case).\n\nThese are disclosed gaps \u2014 the panel's rule presumably allows disclosed gaps (they're \"still disclosed\", meaning known and accepted, with cross-fixture references like m88ktbnd, m88kexchwtraps). A \"floor breach\" would be a reachable cell NOT disclosed. The question: does a clean-sweep mutant exist in the (d) enumeration?\n\nLet me think about the enumeration's categories:\n\n1. Predicates dominating the diff's edited lines up to the function boundary:\n   - switch 1's class labels: e.g., changing which vectors map to which class label. Covered by per-class rows? The class switch: vector -> class. Rows cover classes 1..10 via various routes plus 11/50/127/114/128 for the fallback. A label change, e.g., swapping class labels for vectors 4 and 5? Hmm \u2014 trapfrozen4/5/6/9 pin trap delivery per class. resid rows pin fallback for 11/50/127. What about a label change that maps, say, vector 12..113 to a class? That's \"an exemption of a single residual vector other than 11/50/127\" \u2014 disclosed. Hmm, but what about a switch-1 label change