regress\artifacts\m88kexcdeliver\pass7_panel_20260906_113427\kimi.txt:431:  READ CAREFULLY: the enumerated predicates are the ones DOMINATING the edited lines. If the #502 fix edited (inter alia) the ERROR arm body, then predicates dominating THAT LINE = switch 1's case label for ERROR (and the switch itself). A mutant of the enumerated set = change those dominating predicates: e.g., delete/alter the case label. `implemented = (PSR & SFRZ)` is a mutation of the BODY, not of a dominating predicate. So STRICTLY, it's outside (d)-the-enumeration — as is M_ERRORFRZOFF itself! But pass 6 found M_ERRORFRZOFF and it was accepted as a valid cell ("switch 1's ERROR arm is its own predicate" — codex's framing ELEVATED the arm body to a predicate, i.e., the finding EXPANDED the enumeration by recognizing the body as a predicate). Once accepted and repaired, the class "arm-body predicates" is in the working enumeration. And the repair-chain rule says repairs owe passes scoped to the diff, and classes must be closed.
regress\artifacts\m88kexcdeliver\pass7_panel_20260906_113427\kimi.txt:521:  One more sanity check on the mutant's enumeration membership: "predicates dominating the diff's edited lines up to the function boundary (switch 1's class labels...)". If the #502 fix's edited lines include the ERROR arm body (they must — M_ERRORFRZOFF was measured on the fix), then the arm's eligibility is an edited line whose mutation family was admitted in pass 6. Confirmed in-enumeration by precedent.
regress\artifacts\lcaconfbus1kill\pass2_20260908\seats\ollama_kimi.txt:23:**D4 (the alias binding, answering §F's own question): NOT sufficient as described.** "Bound to `alive2`" rules out died-before-E, but the row still passes if the alias store was *never issued* while the host stayed up (a guest-side skip, an early probe bail on a different branch). Absence-of-print plus host-alive is exactly the vacuity shape §F confesses to, one level up. **Fix:** the positive term must be a *guest-emitted* marker retired after the alias `stq` (a console/UART checkpoint written after the store). If `alive2` is already defined as "guest printed its post-E checkpoint" rather than "host process still exists," then the binding is sufficient — the packet does not say which. READ: not stated. REASONED: insufficient unless that definition holds.
