e-zero!) — which would make some detector rows VACUOUS-by-confusion. This matters for Q4 (vacuity). Also note: even "register unchanged" has a subtle channel: the OLD register value — the probe can preload the register with a sentinel (e.g., 0xA5A5...) and check it survives — that IS observable to the probe. So decline IS observable to the guest-visible state in the form "stale register", even if no fault. Fine.
