RED \u2713. latch two RED \u2713. hwr genctl dcl?? \u2014 does a \"hwr genctl dcl\" row exist? The gate list: \"hwr genctl\", \"hwr genctl lv\" \u2014 no dcl for genctl in the gate list! Hmm: hwr rows with dcl: \"wwr sccerr dcl\", \"hwr sccerr dcl\", \"hwr ipl dcl\". No \"hwr genctl dcl\" \u2014 so the GENCTL hwr announce isn't counted by name... `latch same` covers it. OK so under RET0 at GENCTL, candidate reds: hwr genctl lv, rb genctl, rb vecbase?? \u2014 rb vecbase: session \"st.b VECBASE; st.h GENCTL; ld.bu VECBASE\" \u2014 the st.h to GENCTL FAULTS \u2192 program dies \u2192 readback \"died\" \u2260 0x50 \u2192 RED! The listed string says \"rb genctl,rb genctl lo\" \u2014 maybe \"rb genctl,rb vecbase\" got truncated/miswritten? The table: \"M_RET0_GENCTL 96/101 hwr genctl lv,rb genctl,rb genctl lo,latch two\" \u2014 if rb vecbase also reds that's 5: hwr genctl lv, rb genctl, rb vecbase, rb genctl lo, latch two = 5 \u2713 = 96/101 \u2713!! So the listed string is missing `rb vecbase` (or one of the listed is wrong). Given 96/101 = 5 reds and only 4 named, the packet's part-4 line undercounts its own red list. ALSO \u2014 `acc genctl`? byte \u2713 green. `acc all`: byte \u2713 green (part 4 = 101 rows: acc all existed \u2713; RET0 at GENCTL: acc all session's GENCTL st.b \u2192 guard len!=0? NO \u2014 RET0 mutant is break\u2192return0 at GENCTL's guard: byte write \u2192 guard false \u2192 body \u2713 lands \u2713 green). `op *` rows: put h at ODD blocks \u2192 their own guards (unmutated) \u2192 green \u2713. `latch aba`: A(GENCTL st.h \u2192 announce + FAULT \u2192 program dies \u2192 the rest of the session (VECBASE put h, second GENCTL st.h) \u2014 the guest program died after the first st.h; the debugger commands still run? The session: setup + program([ST_H(6, GENCTL)]) + put h VECBASE + program([ST_H(6, GENCTL)], at=CODE+0x100) \u2014 the FIRST program faults at its st.h \u2192 the put h VECBASE still executes (debugger) \u2192 announce \u2713; the second