\u2713. So reds: hwr genctl lv \u2713, rb genctl \u2713, rb vecbase \u2713, rb genctl lo \u2713, latch two \u2713 = 5 \u2713 96/101 \u2713. The packet names 4, omitting rb vecbase. FLAG \u2713.\n\n**Now M_GROW_IPL part 4: 99/101 \"acc all,acc ipl ro\"** \u2014 101\u221299 = 2 reds \u2713 names 2 \u2713 consistent \u2713. GROW at IPL: st.b at IPL \u2192 declined \u2192 announce \u2192 `acc all` DECL=1 RED \u2713; `acc ipl ro`: st.b at IPL \u2192 declined \u2192 body's print count 0 \u2260 1 \u2192 RED \u2713; `acc ipl... wait acc rows at five blocks (genctl, t2ctl, t2icr, scctx, sccerr) \u2014 no acc ipl readback; acc ipl ro added in pass 4 \u2713. Also `hrd ipl`/`hwr ipl` rows: byte? No \u2014 hrd/hwr ipl are st.h/ld.h \u2713 declined normally \u2713 green. \u2713 2 reds \u2713 consistent \u2713.\n\n**M_LEN8_VECBASE 100/101 latch all d \u2713**: `len != 1' -> `len != 1 && len != 8' at VECBASE: put d at VECBASE \u2192 guard false \u2192 falls \u2192 body: VECBASE = idata & 0xf0 = 0x03 & 0xf0 = 0x00 \u2192 no announce \u2192 latch all d = 11 \u2260 12 RED \u2713 1 red \u2713 consistent \u2713. (Also: does any other row put d at VECBASE? No \u2713.)\n\n**M_LATCH_BIT0 100/101 latch same2 \u2713** derived above \u2713.\n\n**Pass-5 predictions vs measurements:**\n- Section 9 predicted BASE 102/102 \u2014 part 5 measured BASE 118/118 (the instrument grew to 118 because pass-5 added 17 rows, not 1 \u2014 Section 9 was written before the Opus reader's rows were added; the packet doesn't remark the 102\u2192118 growth... Actually Section 9: \"PREDICTIONS for part 5: BASE 102/102\" \u2014 the plan then was one new row (latch all fail) \u2192 102. Then Section 10 (the Opus reader) added 16 more rows \u2192 118. The part-5 BASE measured 118/118 \u2713. The prediction's denominator (102) is stale but that's expected (written before Section 10). Fine.\n- Section 9 predicted M_RET0_VECBASE \u2192 `latch all fail' 1 \u2192 on the 118 instrument: measured latch all fail red \u2713 PLUS rb2 vecbase (unpredicted, underived \u2014 FLAG as above).\n- Section 10 predicted M_QUAL_GENCTL \u2192 rb2 genctl 0xbb \u2014 measured rb2 genctl red \u2713 (value not shown; the packet's tables don't show actual values, only row names \u2713 fine, but the PREDICTION's 0xbb vs the row's 0xaab8\u21920xb8 \u2014 flag as prediction-value defect).\n\n**Q1(d): \"Is any C/W/A cell resting on a cardinality row that a benign session event could inflate or a mutant could preserve?\"**\n\nC = `latch all` counts DECL == 12 over a session of twelve put h. Could a benign event inflate DECL? DECL is the generic decline text \" -- declined.\" \u2014 the note says \"three other devices emit the same suffix, none instantiated on mvme187\" \u2713 so no inflation on mvme187. Could a mutant preserve 12 while breaking? A mutant that makes a block announce TWICE and another ZERO times preserves the count of 12! E.g., bit collision (ALIAS) \u2014 ALIAS drops count (11) \u2713 caught. But a mutant that makes TWO blocks share a bit AND... no: sharing \u2192 11. A mutant that REMOVES one block's guard (DEL at one block: that block lands, no announce \u2192 11 \u2713 caught). A mutant that makes one block announce on every write (flood at one block \u2014 e.g., TEST bit wrong at one block: TEST checks bit X while SET sets bit Y (one-sided translation at ONE block?) \u2014 the helper is SHARED \u2014 can't translate per-block... unless the CALL passes the wrong bit (ALIAS \u2713 caught). What about a mutant that floods at one block and silences at another \u2014 e.g., `bit` argument: block A passes bit_A+1 (translation at ONE call site): A announces every time (TEST bit_A+1 never set \u2014 SET sets bit_A+1? no wait: the call passes bit+1 \u2192 BOTH test and set use bit_A+1 \u2192 translation \u2192 equivalent for A alone (its bit just moves) \u2713 E. But TWO call sites: A passes bit_A+1 = bit_B's... if bit_A+1 happens to be another block's bit \u2192 collision \u2192 latch all = 11 \u2713 caught. Hmm \u2014 what about a mutant that floods A (announce always) and silences B \u2014 sum preserved 12? For the sum to stay 12 with a defect, need +1 and \u22121. A call-site edit changes ONE block's bit \u2192 either translation (E) or collision (\u22121, caught). Can't get +1 from a single call-site bit change. SET-line `|=' \u2192 `=': latch all: A,B,C...: each block announces once \u2713 12 \u2014 the FIRST write to each block announces \u2713 \u2014 latch all stays 12 GREEN under `=' \u2014 but caught by latch aba \u2713 (that's WHY latch aba exists \u2713). So the C cells (ALIAS/SWAP at various arms) rest on latch all \u2014 fine given latch aba covers assignment. But: **SWAP at arms marked C: SWAP = `len != 1' -> `idata > 0xff'** \u2014 at arms whose rows only ever write values > 0xff, the guard stays true on those rows; the latch-all session writes 0x0003 \u2192 lands \u2192 count 11 \u2713 caught \u2713. But ALSO: the LANDED 0x03 into the arm \u2014 e.g., SWAP at SCCICR: latch all's put h 0x0003 at SCCICR \u2192 lands \u2192 SCCICR = 0x03 & 0x1f \u2192 reassert \u2014 harmless, count 11 \u2192 RED \u2713. \u2713 fine.\n\nW = latch all w (word writes, 0x00000003): LEN2 at any arm \u2192 word lands silently \u2192 11 \u2713 caught. Could a benign event inflate? DECL count over the whole transcript \u2014 the session is twelve put w only \u2713 no other wide writes \u2713. A mutant preserving 12: `len == 2' at one arm \u2192 that arm's WORD lands \u2192 11 \u2713 caught. \u2713 fine.\n\nA/C: acc rows + acc all: GROW at any arm \u2192 acc all = 1 \u2713. Could acc all be 1 benignly? Twelve st.b, one reassert... DECL only from guards \u2713. A mutant preserving 0: GROW at an arm whose byte writes... all twelve st.b hit all twelve blocks \u2713 any GROW reds \u2713 measured (95/96 part 3c at PSCALEADJ \u2713, M_GROW_IPL 99/101 \u2713).\n\nOne more cardinality risk: **`latch all fail` counts \"failed ]\" at 0 over the latch-all session** \u2014 could a BENIGN event print \"failed ]\" in that session? The session is twelve put h at PCC2 offsets. On the fix, all decline \u2192 return normally \u2192 no \"failed\" \u2713. But \u2014 what about OTHER memory failures in the same pty transcript? The session is JUST the twelve puts (no setup/program) \u2713 per the diff: `session([\"put h 0x%x, 0x0003\" % (PCC2 + o) for _, o in BLOCKS12])` \u2713 nothing else \u2713. OK.\n\nAnd **the `latch all` DECL count over twelve put h of value 0x0003**: under the FIX, each declines \u2713 12. Under a mutant that makes one arm LAND (e.g., SWAP at TxCTL: 0x0003 fits byte \u2192 lands \u2192 0x03 into T2CTL \u2192 count 11 \u2713 RED \u2713). \u2713.\n\n**Q1 \"Is the DOMAIN now the whole of what the fix introduced -- the twelve guards, the helper, and nothing else?\"** \u2014 What the fix introduced: (i) twelve guard blocks (covered: 9 shapes \u00d7 12 blocks + T1 labels + widths + QUAL + FAULT); (ii) the helper (TEST/SET/args \u2014 covered, with NAME gap disclosed); (iii) the direction split's READ-accept path \u2014 the memcpy above the switch serving reads: NOT the fix's lines (pre-existing) but the fix's CONTRACT depends on it (\"READS ACCEPT -- the memcpy above the switch already served them\") \u2014 is the memcpy pinned? \"the value a wide READ composes -- lane order and width\" is a CATCHES bullet \u2713 (val rows? \"val h genctl\", \"val w sccerr\" + hrd * lv 0x5a5a5a5a...). Hmm \u2014 the wide-read VALUE rows: hrd * lv expects 0x5a5a5a5a \u2014 which is SCRATCH pattern \u2014 as noted that might be a liveness-only value... wait: program([I_ST_SCR, LD_H(4, off), I_LD_SCR]) \u2014 hmm, what are these? I_ST_SCR stores r4 (0x5a5a5a5a from setup?) to SCRATCH; LD_H(4, off) loads halfword from PCC2+off into r4; I_LD_SCR loads SCRATCH back into r4?? Then r4 = 0x5a5a5a5a always \u2014 making `hrd * lv` a LIVENESS check only. Hmm \u2014 OR I_ST_SCR/I_LD_SCR store/load FLAGS (like storing the register state to survive)... \"0x5a5a5a5a\" \u2014 setup() presumably sets r4 = 0x5a5a5a5a and SCRATCH = 0x5a5a5a5a pattern. If the pcc2 register read served by memcpy returns pcctwo_reg[off..off+1] \u2014 e.g., GENCTL was set to 0x82 earlier \u2192 ld.h at GENCTL \u2192 r4 = 0x82?? but the row expects 0x5a5a5a5a \u2014 so the program must restore r4 from scratch AFTER the load \u2014 meaning the load's value is NOT checked!! Wait: [I_ST_SCR, LD_H(4, off), I_LD_SCR]: st r4\u2192scratch; ld.h \u2192 r4 = mem[PCC2+off] (16-bit \u2192 r4 = 0x??82 zero-extended? or sign?); ld scratch \u2192 r4 = 0x5a5a5a5a. print r4 \u2192 0x5a5a5a5a ALWAYS (if the program completes). So `hrd genctl lv` checks the program RAN TO COMPLETION (didn't fault), not the read value. Then which row checks the wide READ's composed VALUE? \"val h genctl\" / \"val w sccerr\" \u2713 presumably those. OK \u2014 the packet doesn't inline those sessions \u2014 can't verify the read-compose channel. NOT CHECKABLE \u2014 fine, they're original 60-row rows.\n\nHmm wait \u2014 actually, why would the program do I_ST_SCR then LD_H then I_LD_SCR? Maybe I_ST_SCR = \"store r4 to scratch\" is to SAVE r4 (0x5a5a5a5a from setup) and I_LD_SCR = \"load flags\"? Actually in these m88k probes: I_ST_SCR might store r4 to SCRATCH; I_LD_SCR might load from SCRATCH into r4? Then the LD_H result is overwritten \u2014 odd. OR: I_ST_SCR stores r4 to scratch; LD_H(4, off) \u2192 r4 = halfword; I_LD_SCR loads SCRATCH into r1?? I don't know. The expectation 0x5a5a5a5a for a HALFWORD read of GENCTL \u2014 if GENCTL holds 0x82 and VECBASE 0x50 (set in earlier sessions? NO \u2014 fresh session! In `hrd genctl`'s session, GENCTL holds its INITIAL value (probably 0) \u2192 ld.h \u2192 r4 = 0x0000 \u2192 not 0x5a5a5a5a). So `hrd * lv` must be checking something else \u2014 the SCRATCH round-trip \u2014 i.e., liveness \u2713. Fine \u2014 as recorded: \"...and runs on\" \u2713 the row's own description says RUNS ON \u2713 liveness \u2713 consistent.\n\nHmm \u2014 so where is the WIDE-READ VALUE pinned? \"val h genctl\" \u2014 from the original 60-row: not inlined. OK not checkable.\n\n**(b) more S-cell checks:**\n\n- PSCALEADJ DEL S: guard deleted at PSCALEADJ \u2192 put h 0x0303 \u2192 body prints \"ignored (value 0x0303?)\" \u2014 count \"PSCALEADJ ignored\" = 1 \u2260 0 \u2192 `op pscale noig` RED \u2713. But ALSO \u2014 DEL at PSCALEADJ removes the ANNOUNCE \u2192 `op pscale dcl` counts DECL == 1 \u2192 under DEL: no decline \u2192 0 \u2260 1 \u2192 RED TOO \u2713. S justified (channel = the noig row, same as FALL's \u2014 FALL measured M at PSCALEADJ? Table: PSCALEADJ FALL M \u2713 measured part 2 (rb/op pscale noig \u2014 part 2's rows \u2713). \u2713.\n- TxCTL DEL S: guard deleted \u2192 st.h lands \u2192 rb t2ctl RED \u2713 (measured FALL at TxCTL part 3b \u2713 same landing \u2713 S fine).\n- GENCTL KILL S: kill at GENCTL \u2192 hwr genctl (exit0?) \u2192 guest dies \u2192 how = died/exit1 \u2192 RED \u2713 survival channel \u2713 (KILL at GENCTL measured at 78? part 1 \u2713 M/S fine).\n- IPL LEN S: `len > 2' at IPL: st.h IPL \u2192 falls \u2192 body prints \"read-only ignored\" ONCE (per process) \u2192 `hwr ipl noig` counts 0 \u2260 1 \u2192 RED \u2713 (and `hwr ipl dcl` = 0 \u2260 1 RED too \u2713). \u2713 S fine.\n- MASK LEN2 W: word put w 0x00000003 at MASK \u2192 guard `len == 2' false (len 4) \u2192 lands \u2192 (uint8_t)3 = 3 \u2192 MASK = 3 \u2192 no announce \u2192 latch all w = 11 RED \u2713 W fine.\n- VECBASE LEN2 W \u2713 same.\n\n**SCCERR GROW A/C** \u2713 acc all \u2713.\n\n**GENCTL SWAP M** \u2014 measured (table 1 M_?? \"rb genctl lo\" was written \"before the repair table ran; the table says whether it kills\" \u2014 part 2? \"M_IDATA_GENCTL 80/82\" (part 2) \u2713 measured \u2713.\n\n**Now, the \"five new rows\" vs part 4 measuring \"the five mutants\"** \u2713 consistent (part 4: 5 mutants: M_LEN8_VECBASE, M_LATCH_ASSIGN, M_LATCH_BIT0, M_GROW_IPL, M_RET0_GENCTL \u2713 all killed \u2713 96/101 etc. \u2014 wait \"the five mutants\" measured in part 4 \u2713 all show reds \u2713 good).\n\n**Pass-5's mutants: part 5 measures M_RET0_VECBASE (116/118), M_TEST_EQ (117/118), M_QUAL_GENCTL (117/118); part 5b: M_QUAL_ALL (107/118), M_NOWRITECHK_GENCTL (117/118)** \u2014 all killed \u2713 no sweeps \u2713 the class is closed on the measured set \u2713.\n\n**Now the QUAL red-value check for `rb2 mask`**: pre 0x12, two put h 0xaab8 at MASK \u2192 QUAL: second lands \u2192 MASK = (uint8_t)0xaab8 = 0xb8 (MASK stores byte unmasked) \u2192 \"0xb8\" \u2260 \"0x12\" RED \u2713 (part 5b lists rb2 mask \u2713).\n\n**rb2 genctl on the FIX**: two st.h 0xaab8 \u2192 both declined \u2192 0x82 \u2713 green \u2713. NOTE \u2014 GENCTL stores the byte AND reasserts \u2014 under QUAL the second st.h lands 0xb8 \u2192 GENCTL = 0xb8 \u2192 reassert with 0xb8: bit 0x04 (C040) \u2014 0xb8 = 0b10111000 \u2192 bit 0x04 CLEAR \u2713 no c040 kill \u2713 (the rows keep 0x04 clear as noted \u2713 0xb8 & 0x04 = 0 \u2713; 0xaab8 & 0x04 = 0 \u2713; 0xbb & 0x04 = 0? 0xbb = 10111011 \u2192 bit 0x04 = 0 \u2713 \u2014 so even Opus's 0xbb landing is safe \u2713).\n\n**One more enumeration axis: the two", "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 361680830056}
