regress\artifacts\sgirebufuninit\pass1_panel\grok.txt:196:`memset` does not stop `default:` overwriting with `random()`. Removing `random()` does not fill `buf[4..7]`. A shared “deterministic across runs” oracle **misses stable-stack uninit** (wrong every run, same every run) and is the vacuity-floor problem, not a saving. `sgirandomcolour` still has `witness: null`. Same detector, no new oracle: false.
